(6336460, 937339, 54645, '<td valign="top">A perfect composition, which I know is stating the obvious, but why not start with the easy part. I was initially drawn by the tones and smooth color in the sky.  I like that you kept the distortion of the horizon, but I will add a critique that you went to far with the sharpening. Such a smooth and tranquil moment, it''s perfectly acceptable to leave an image naturally sharp (or soft in the land of DPC!). 7<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-03-08 00:05:59.</i></td>', 'A perfect composition, which I know is stating the obvious, but why not start with the easy part. I was initially drawn by the tones and smooth color in the sky.  I like that you kept the distortion of the horizon, but I will add a critique that you went to far with the sharpening. Such a smooth and tranquil moment, it''s perfectly acceptable to leave an image naturally sharp (or soft in the land of DPC!). 7', '2011-03-01 00:52:16.000000', '2011-03-08 00:05:59.000000', 1),
