(6345682, 938313, 40718, '<td valign="top">Wow!  You have outdone yourself on this one.  I''m working out the shot in my mind and I can''t quite do it.  Very well done.</td>', 'Wow!  You have outdone yourself on this one.  I''m working out the shot in my mind and I can''t quite do it.  Very well done.', '2011-03-08 15:30:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(6345686, 938313, 30861, '<td valign="top">It''s good to see you moving away from the featureless backgrounds, which I always thought were limiting your shots. This one is exceptionally nice. Apparently there are some voters who don''t recognize the evolution and think this is the same ol'' same ol'', as evidenced by the 18 low votes, but in the end your distribution is heavily skewed towards the positive. Well done!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-03-08 17:09:30.</i></td>', 'It''s good to see you moving away from the featureless backgrounds, which I always thought were limiting your shots. This one is exceptionally nice. Apparently there are some voters who don''t recognize the evolution and think this is the same ol'' same ol'', as evidenced by the 18 low votes, but in the end your distribution is heavily skewed towards the positive. Well done!', '2011-03-08 15:32:15.000000', '2011-03-08 17:09:30.000000', 0),
(6345694, 937010, 30861, '<td valign="top">I''ve had a couple good finishes with these animals as well: 10th and 11th. Sadly, mine aren''t around anymore; they''ve moved off-cape. People seem to like these whimsical beasts.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=894213" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1231/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_894213.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1231/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_894213.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1231/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_894213.jpg"/></a> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=797325" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1046/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_797325.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1046/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_797325.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1046/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_797325.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I like your shot the best of these 3 :-) How about showing people the original version, so they can see why you cropped to one horn?<br/></td>', 'I''ve had a couple good finishes with these animals as well: 10th and 11th. Sadly, mine aren''t around anymore; they''ve moved off-cape. People seem to like these whimsical beasts.    I like your shot the best of these 3 :-) How about showing people the original version, so they can see why you cropped to one horn?', '2011-03-08 15:36:48.000000', NULL, 0),
