(6347111, 938313, 61961, '<td valign="top">Fantastic.  I gave this an 8 on first review and would have bumped it up if I''d gone through the entries a second time as I often do.  <br/> <br/>So you bought the materials and built the setup?  Does that mean you are on you knees in a fake room you built?  OMG, I''ll never compete with that much prep, even though in a case like this I see it is worth the effort!</td>', 'Fantastic.  I gave this an 8 on first review and would have bumped it up if I''d gone through the entries a second time as I often do.   So you bought the materials and built the setup?  Does that mean you are on you knees in a fake room you built?  OMG, I''ll never compete with that much prep, even though in a case like this I see it is worth the effort!', '2011-03-09 15:33:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(6347117, 938313, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by citymars:</b></div><hr/><i> Fantastic.  I gave this an 8 on first review and would have bumped it up if I''d gone through the entries a second time as I often do.  <br/> <br/>So you bought the materials and built the setup?  Does that mean you are on you knees in a fake room you built?  OMG, I''ll never compete with that much prep, even though in a case like this I see it is worth the effort! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you!<br/>However, the fake room solution wouldn''t work here, the tea wouldn''t flow to the "ground". So the trick is something different this time ;-)</td>', 'Originally posted by citymars: Fantastic.  I gave this an 8 on first review and would have bumped it up if I''d gone through the entries a second time as I often do.   So you bought the materials and built the setup?  Does that mean you are on you knees in a fake room you built?  OMG, I''ll never compete with that much prep, even though in a case like this I see it is worth the effort!   Thank you!However, the fake room solution wouldn''t work here, the tea wouldn''t flow to the "ground". So the trick is something different this time ;-)', '2011-03-09 15:36:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(6347125, 938313, 61961, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> Thank you!  However, the fake room solution wouldn''t work here, the tea wouldn''t flow to the "ground". So the trick is something different this time ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hmm, so much for my theory, I figured you the "flowing tea" was plastic or something!  Keep up the great work.</td>', 'Originally posted by gyaban: Thank you!  However, the fake room solution wouldn''t work here, the tea wouldn''t flow to the "ground". So the trick is something different this time ;-)  Hmm, so much for my theory, I figured you the "flowing tea" was plastic or something!  Keep up the great work.', '2011-03-09 15:41:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6347142, 938313, 114969, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by citymars:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by gyaban:</b></div><hr/><i> Thank you!  However, the fake room solution wouldn''t work here, the tea wouldn''t flow to the "ground". So the trick is something different this time ;-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Hmm, so much for my theory, I figured you the "flowing tea" was plastic or something!  Keep up the great work. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Tea is absolutely real. And hot :-) I drilled holes in both the cup and the spoon and screwed them together, but it wasn''t very waterproof: I regularly had hot tea on the fingers, which was one of numerous reasons for a missed attempt.</td>', 'Originally posted by citymars: Originally posted by gyaban: Thank you!  However, the fake room solution wouldn''t work here, the tea wouldn''t flow to the "ground". So the trick is something different this time ;-)  Hmm, so much for my theory, I figured you the "flowing tea" was plastic or something!  Keep up the great work.   Tea is absolutely real. And hot :-) I drilled holes in both the cup and the spoon and screwed them together, but it wasn''t very waterproof: I regularly had hot tea on the fingers, which was one of numerous reasons for a missed attempt.', '2011-03-09 15:48:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6347277, 938313, 87252, '<td valign="top">This is amaaaazing - it hurts my brain trying to do the mental gymnastics to work out how you did it.</td>', 'This is amaaaazing - it hurts my brain trying to do the mental gymnastics to work out how you did it.', '2011-03-09 18:06:11.000000', NULL, 0),
